- Task 1: complete (commits 5c7c08c..4cc17c4, review clean; minor: later tasks must not edit baseline tests)
- Task 2: complete (commits 4cc17c4..446cec7, review clean; eol lf verified; 51 real values checked, 0 in repo)
- Task 3: dispatched (Opus), BASE 446cec7
  - Task 3 report DONE_WITH_CONCERNS (ced4ff4f). Ruling: accept the spec-exact thinking-only rule with a tentative message and `Translator::restore` rollback — the plan's per-source look-ahead differs from the spec on two valid shapes (F7) — cost if wrong: more code to maintain; the Opus reviewer checks the restore invariant.
  - Ruling: accept `SortKey { At(u64,u8), BeforeFirstToolUse }`, one shared key for all text blocks of a group, and skip-with-debug for a `tool_use` position with no call id — the spec does not decide these; they keep its keys — cost: small.
  - Task 3 review (Opus): Approved, 0 Critical/Important, 4 Minor.
  - Ruling: reviewer Minor 1 is raised to Important — a thinking-only source message that joins an earlier round (SMA-834 join, or after a rollback) attaches thinking to a wire message whose tool_use blocks come from another response; `main` never sends that shape and no probe covers it (Anti-goal) — fix: a source message whose own span (its ToolUse parts plus its following ToolCall items) has no text and no tool_use drops its thinking blocks wherever it lands; spec rule 5 (wire level) still applies on top. This changes F7 shape 2 ("a later nested tool_use joins the thinking-only message") from kept to dropped, which is closer to `main`. — cost if wrong: thinking dropped in a rare shape where the API would accept it.
  - Task 3: minor (deferred): sort_groups is O(groups x blocks) per wire message (reviewer Minor 2).
  - Task 3: minor (deferred): debug logs repeat after a rollback (reviewer Minor 4).
  - Task 3: Minor 3 (debug_assert that no tentative message is active in restore) goes into fix round 1.
- Task 3: fix round 1/5 (Finding A source rule + B invariant done by implementer; 1 related case open — thinking-only item whose own call lands in a later wire message still keeps thinking in an earlier joined round; commits ced4ff4..bff1a6d)
  - Ruling: generalize — a source message keeps its thinking blocks only if the wire message they land in also holds a text or tool_use block from the same source message; otherwise they are dropped (the request then equals the request without the Anthropic parts for that item). This subsumes spec rule 5 and the round-1 source rule — the Anti-goal forbids shapes `main` never sends — cost if wrong: thinking dropped in rare shapes.
